  "solution": {
    "text": "From the figure, it is clear that the plate is placed in an external electric field. Let the electric field due to plate be E, and E<sub>0</sub> is the external electric field.<br /><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0031008_Ans.jpg\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 100px;\" /><br /><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo> <mtext>E</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>2</mn> <msup> <mo>V m</mo> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>E</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mo>-</mo> <mtext>E</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> <msup> <mo>V m</mo> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Solving equations, E = 2 V m<sup>-1</sup> and E<sub>0</sub> = 10 V m<sup>-1</sup><br /><br />Now, electric field due to plate <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo> <mfrac> <mrow> <mi>σ</mi> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> <msub> <mi>ε</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </math><br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>∴&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo> <mi>σ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <msub> <mi>ε</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>",
